<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John I Albert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1459–1501</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Jan Olbracht</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John I Albert was a Jagiellonian king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1492 to 1501, son of Casimir IV. He strengthened the rights of the nobility in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> and led a failed campaign into Moldavia in 1497. He bought the Silesian duchy of Zator in 1494 and incorporated the Masovian duchy of Płock in 1495 after its last duke died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-i-albert.jpg" alt="John I Albert" width="320" height="514" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anonymous (graphic from book by Zygmunt Gloger (1845-1910)) derivative work: Airam57 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PL_Gloger-Encyklopedja_staropolska_ilustrowana_T.4_454a.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
